ComfyUI-BCNodes — libs/dype/

This directory contains code derived from ComfyUI-DyPE
(https://github.com/wildminder/ComfyUI-DyPE), by wildminder and the ComfyUI-DyPE contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE in this directory). The sources are the
files src/rope.py (rope.py), src/base.py (DyPEBasePosEmbed: its NTK and dynamic PI branches and its
attention-scale decay) and the rotation layout of src/models/zimage.py and src/models/qwen.py
(embed.py) at commit 266405844738da9f16e8a072482320168a17c494 (2026-10-24, version 2.20.0).

ComfyUI-DyPE implements DyPE, Dynamic Position Extrapolation, by Noam Issachar, Guy Yariv and
co-authors (https://github.com/guyyariv/DyPE), over the NTK-by-parts interpolation of YaRN.

Changes made in ComfyUI-BCNodes (rope.py):
- The frequencies are computed in float64 on the caller's device, as ComfyUI core's rope computes
  them, with core's linspace exponents; the original computed them in a dtype its caller picked
  (bfloat16 on CUDA for Z-Image).
- The functions return the frequency table only. The angles, their cos / sin and the attention
  scale are taken by the caller; the original returned cos / sin repeat-interleaved.
- DyPE's modulation exponent (dype_scale * t ** dype_exponent) is computed by the caller and passed
  in as k_t.
- The NTK-by-parts blend shared by YaRN and Vision YaRN is one function (_parts); the
  correction-range and ramp helpers are restated with the same values.
- The decaying attention scale of the models' Vision YaRN, 1 + c ln(scale) t_norm^dype_exponent,
  is one function (attention_scale) with the model's coefficient c (Z-Image 0.05, Qwen-Image 0.1).

Changes made in ComfyUI-BCNodes (embed.py):
- One embedder module per sampling step, with the step's scale, timestep and settings fixed, in
  place of the original's state set on a shared embedder; the models' embedders (models/<model>/dype/)
  subclass it with their Vision YaRN and YaRN tables.
- The rotations are built in ComfyUI core's EmbedND layout from float64 tables on a device that
  supports it (the CPU otherwise) and returned in float32, as core's rope; the original computed
  cos / sin repeat-interleaved in bfloat16 on CUDA and de-interleaved them per model.
- The method `pi` scales the image positions by scale ** k_t for every model (DY-PI, the
  original's base-class branch).
